---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { fetchLatestGhwmTag, getInstallCommands } from '../../lib/github';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const latestTag = await fetchLatestGhwmTag();
const installCommands = getInstallCommands(latestTag);

const manifestExample = `source: ghwfxlab/ghwm-registry
workflows:
  - name: super-linter
    version: 1.0.0
  - name: auto-assign-pr
    version: 1.0.0
    update-triggers: true
    update-config-files: true`;

const bumpExample = `workflows:
  - name: super-linter
-    version: 1.0.0
+    version: 1.1.0`;

const customSourceExample = `source: ghwfxlab/ghwm-registry
workflows:
  - name: super-linter
    version: 1.0.0
  - name: internal-deploy
    version: 2.1.0
    source: my-org/my-registry`;

const renovateExample = `{
  "extends": ["github>ghwfxlab/ghwm-registry//renovate/default.json"]
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart"
  description="Install the ghwm CLI, describe your workflows in ghwm.yml, and install them into your repository."
  current="quickstart"
>
  <p>
    This guide installs the CLI and adds two workflows to a repository. It takes a few minutes.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Install the CLI</h2>
  <p>Pin the CLI to the latest tagged release (recommended):</p>
  <CodeBlock code={installCommands['uv-pinned']} />
  <p>
    Prefer another tool? Use <code>{installCommands['pipx']}</code> or{' '}
    <code>{installCommands['pip']}</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Create <code>ghwm.yml</code></h2>
  <p>Add this file to the root of your repository:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={manifestExample} label="ghwm.yml" />
  <p>
    <code>source</code> is the registry repository, and each workflow needs a <code>name</code> and an exact{' '}
    <code>version</code>. Per-workflow options such as <code>update-triggers</code> and{' '}
    <code>update-config-files</code> are described in the <a href={withBase('/docs/manifest/')}>manifest reference</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Install the workflows</h2>
  <CodeBlock code="ghwm install" />
  <p>
    Commit the files it generates, including <code>ghwm.lock</code>. Some workflows need secrets or variables;
    check each package's page in the <a href={withBase('/registry')}>registry</a> for its setup.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Update workflows</h2>
  <p>Bump the version in <code>ghwm.yml</code>, then refresh:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={bumpExample} label="ghwm.yml (diff)" />
  <CodeBlock code="ghwm update" />

  <h2>5. Remove a workflow</h2>
  <p>
    Delete its entry from <code>ghwm.yml</code> and run <code>ghwm install</code>. See the{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/ghwfxlab/ghwm#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ghwm CLI readme</a>{' '}
    for all commands and pruning options.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Keep versions current with Renovate</h2>
  <p>Add the preset to <code>renovate.json</code> to receive pull requests when new package versions ship:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={renovateExample} label="renovate.json" />

  <h2 id="custom-registries">Custom registries</h2>
  <p>
    You are not limited to this registry. The <code>source</code> key in <code>ghwm.yml</code> names the registry
    repository in <code>owner/repository</code> format, and packages are resolved from GitHub Packages as{' '}
    <code>@owner/name</code>. Create your own from the{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/ghwfxlab/ghwm-registry-template" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ghwm-registry-template</a>{' '}
    repository template; see <a href={withBase('/docs/writing-a-package/')}>Writing a package</a> for the layout.
  </p>
  <p>To pull one workflow from a different registry, override <code>source</code> on that entry:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={customSourceExample} label="ghwm.yml" />
  <p>
    For authentication, telemetry, and other CLI behavior, see the{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/ghwfxlab/ghwm#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ghwm CLI readme</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
